# TypeScript Standards

## Purpose

Keep TypeScript uniform, strict, and dual-target (ESM + CJS) across every package.

## Why it exists

The whole monorepo shares one strict compiler baseline
([base.json](mdc:shared/typescript-config/base.json)) and ships via `tsup` to Node 18+.
Consistent typing and naming is what lets `@lensjs/core` primitives be reused everywhere
without friction, and what keeps public `.d.ts` output correct for consumers.

## Compiler baseline (do not weaken)

`strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `noImplicitOverride`, `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`,
`skipLibCheck`. Emit is owned by `tsup`, so the shared config sets `noEmit: true`.
Each package extends a semantically-named preset (`core.json`, `express.json`,
`fastify.json`, `handlers.json`) that today just re-extends `base.json` — extend the named
one anyway so it stays a stable per-package extension point.

## Mandatory rules

- Use `import type { ... }` for type-only imports (`verbatimModuleSyntax` is on in several
  packages and the UI).
- Prefix Node built-ins: `import path from "node:path"`, `import { randomUUID } from "node:crypto"`.
- Give exported functions and public class methods explicit return types.
- Respect `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`: guard array/record access; do not blindly `!`-assert.
- Handle every promise: `await` it, or explicitly `void` a fire-and-forget call (adapters use
  `void this.watchQueries(...)`). Never leave a floating promise.
- Use `override` when overriding a base method (`noImplicitOverride`) — see
  [better_sqlite.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/stores/better_sqlite.ts).
- Avoid `any`. If unavoidable at an internal boundary, isolate it and comment why. NEVER widen
  a public type to `any`.

## Naming & file placement

- File names: `snake_case.ts` (`cache_watcher.ts`, `api_controller.ts`, `async_context.ts`,
  `event_emitter.ts`). Single-word files stay lowercase (`prisma.ts`, `compose.ts`).
- Classes / types / interfaces / enums: `PascalCase`. Variables / functions: `camelCase`.
- Enums use the `...Enum` suffix (`WatcherTypeEnum`) with string values.
- Abstract base classes live in `abstracts/`; class mixins in `mixins/`; pure helpers in
  `utils/`; DI/context in `context/`.
- React UI files are the exception: PascalCase `.tsx` for components (see `frontend.mdc`).

## Generics & composition

- Prefer generics over `any` for reusable shapes: `Paginator<T>`, `ApiResponse<T>`,
  `TypedEventEmitter<T>`, the overloaded `compose<>()`
  ([compose.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/utils/compose.ts)).
- Derive constrained unions from core types instead of restating them, e.g.
  `Extract<SqlQueryType, "mysql" | "postgresql" | ...>` in
  [handlers types/query.ts](mdc:packages/handlers/src/types/query.ts).
- Prefer composition (mixins via `compose()`) and small abstract contracts over deep
  inheritance trees.

## Error handling & async

- Instrumentation must never throw into the host app: wrap capture in try/catch and
  `console.error` on failure (see adapter `finalizeRequestLog`), never rethrow.
- Normalize errors through [lensExceptionUtils](mdc:packages/core/src/utils/exception.ts)
  (`constructErrorObject`) rather than hand-building exception payloads.

## Logging & comments

- Logging is `console.*` only, and only for genuinely exceptional/operational events
  (queue overflow warning, DB connect, save failure). No logging framework, no debug spam.
- Do not write comments that narrate code. Comment only non-obvious intent/constraints.
- Add JSDoc to exported utility functions (mirror the JSDoc in
  [exception.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/utils/exception.ts) and
  [utils/index.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/utils/index.ts)).

## Style (Prettier defaults, no committed lint for backend)

Double quotes, semicolons, 2-space indent, trailing commas in multiline literals.

```typescript
// GOOD
import type { RouteDefinition } from "../types";
import path from "node:path";

export function normalizePath(p: string): string {
  return p.startsWith("/") ? p : `/${p}`;
}
```

## AI must never

- Disable or loosen a strict compiler flag to make code compile.
- Introduce a floating promise or swallow one silently without `void`/`await`.
- Add `any` to a public/exported type.
- Rename files to `camelCase`/`kebab-case` — backend files are `snake_case.ts`.
